    <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap page-hero-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow">Rumman · Guided Intelligent ERP</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="hero-lead">Rumman was designed with a local-first architecture: detailed ERP operations remain primarily on the smartphone.</p></div><p class="effective-date">Effective: July 21, 2026. Last updated: July 22, 2026.</p></div></section>
    <div class="wrap legal-layout">
      <aside class="legal-toc" aria-label="On this page"><strong>On this page</strong><ol><li><a href="#controller">Who controls the data</a></li><li><a href="#local">Data on the device</a></li><li><a href="#cloud">Data processed in the cloud</a></li><li><a href="#ai">AI Assistant</a></li><li><a href="#purposes">Purposes</a></li><li><a href="#permissions">Permissions</a></li><li><a href="#providers">Providers and transfers</a></li><li><a href="#retention">Retention and deletion</a></li><li><a href="#rights">Your rights</a></li><li><a href="#children">Children and changes</a></li></ol></aside>
      <article class="legal-document">
        <section class="legal-section" id="controller"><h2>1. Who controls the data</h2><p>Rumman Guided Intelligent ERP (“Rumman”) is responsible for the processing described in this policy. Public contact: <a href="mailto:e-mail@rumman.app.br">e-mail@rumman.app.br</a>. Developer: <a href="https://pascoal.eti.br" rel="external noopener">Pascoal Eti</a>; technical contact: <a href="mailto:devs@pascoal.eti.br">devs@pascoal.eti.br</a>.</p></section>
        <section class="legal-section" id="local"><h2>2. Data stored on the device</h2><p>Customer records, detailed financial entries, categories, complete Assistant conversations, Assistant memory, customer photos, scanned documents, recognized text and attached files remain in the app's private storage. This data is not automatically sent to the cloud.</p><p>When device backup is enabled, Android may include the <code>rumman.db</code> operational database in the user's private Google Account backup for restoration or device transfer. This process is controlled by Android and does not use Rumman infrastructure.</p></section>
        <section class="legal-section" id="cloud"><h2>3. Data processed in the cloud</h2><ul><li><strong>Account:</strong> name, email address, identifier, login provider and technical security data in Firebase Authentication.</li><li><strong>Profile and summary:</strong> profile and a dashboard summary, including customer count, pending tasks, aggregate monthly balance and a business health indicator, in Cloud Firestore.</li><li><strong>Protection:</strong> integrity token and technical app/device information in Firebase App Check and Google Play Integrity.</li><li><strong>Diagnostics:</strong> crash reports, app state, device model/system and installation identifiers in Firebase Crashlytics.</li><li><strong>Subscription and limits:</strong> account identifier, plan status and monthly AI counters in Cloudflare D1.</li></ul></section>
        <section class="legal-section" id="ai"><h2>4. AI Assistant</h2><p>Only when the user taps send does the app transmit the request text, a limited portion of recent history, configured memory and text from selected attachments to the Cloudflare gateway. The gateway does not store prompts or responses in D1; Cloudflare Workers AI processes them to generate the response. Avoid entering unnecessary personal or confidential information.</p></section>
        <section class="legal-section" id="purposes"><h2>5. Purposes</h2><p>Data is processed to create and protect the account, deliver requested features, synchronize the summary, enforce plan limits, diagnose failures, prevent fraud and comply with legal obligations. Rumman does not sell data and does not display ads.</p></section>
        <section class="legal-section" id="permissions"><h2>6. Permissions</h2><p>The camera is requested to scan documents and capture images selected by the user. Internet access is used for login, synchronization, protection, diagnostics and AI. The app does not request location, contacts, microphone or SMS permissions.</p></section>
        <section class="legal-section" id="providers"><h2>7. Providers, security and transfers</h2><p>Google Firebase, Google Play Integrity and Cloudflare act as infrastructure providers. Data may be processed outside Brazil with applicable contractual and technical safeguards. Traffic uses HTTPS.</p></section>
        <section class="legal-section" id="retention"><h2>8. Retention and deletion</h2><p>Local data remains until the user deletes it, the account is deleted, Android app data is cleared or the app is uninstalled. Account, profile, summary, plan and counters remain while the account is active and are removed when deletion is completed, except for retention strictly required by law, security or fraud prevention. Crash reports are retained only for the period needed for diagnostics and under the provider's retention rules.</p><p>Android Auto Backup is subject to platform rules: a total limit of 25 MB per app and execution usually once a day when system conditions are met. Credentials, tokens, cache, scanned images and attachments are excluded. Restoration depends on the same Google Account and the device backup settings.</p></section>
        <section class="legal-section" id="rights"><h2>9. Your rights</h2><p>The user may request confirmation of processing, access, correction, information, portability where applicable and deletion. In the app: <strong>Profile → Privacy and data</strong>. Outside the app: use the <a href="/excluir-conta">public deletion page</a> or email <a href="mailto:e-mail@rumman.app.br">e-mail@rumman.app.br</a>.</p></section>
        <section class="legal-section" id="children"><h2>10. Children and changes</h2><p>Rumman is a business management product and is not directed at children. Material changes to this policy will be communicated in the app or on the public page, with the date updated.</p></section>
